**This may be a medical emergency. Please get urgent medical help now: call 999 or go to your nearest A&E. If you are unsure, contact NHS 111 (call 111 or visit 111.nhs.uk) straight away.**

- Do not wait for symptoms to appear before getting help.
- If you can, take the iron tablet bottle or packaging with you, so the medical team can see exactly what was taken and how much.
- If someone is with you, tell them what has happened so they can help you get care.

I record and cite sources rather than give medical advice, so I cannot say what will happen to you. The one directly relevant sourced fact is that the NHS states "very high doses of iron can be fatal." That is why getting emergency care now matters.

If you took the tablets because you wanted to harm yourself, you can also talk to Samaritans at any time, day or night, on 116 123. Getting emergency medical help comes first.

