On the UK guidance you asked about, the NHS states that "Taking 17mg or less a day of iron supplements is unlikely to cause any harm. But continue taking a higher dose if advised to by a GP." The NHS also states that "Side effects of taking high doses (over 20mg) of iron include: constipation, feeling sick, being sick, stomach pain." The NHS sources do not describe the 17mg figure as a formal "upper limit," and they do not mention the US figure. No NICE or BNF source was found on this point.

The NHS also states that ferrous sulfate and ferrous fumarate, which are iron medicines, are available on prescription and to buy from pharmacies. No BNF legal category was found.

